# {{ .computed.app_title }}

An app-ade project: the shared Substrate agentic app host with its own identity and SQLite,
app-shell, and the ADE packages, so a person and an agent work over the same surface. The
person and the agent see the same thing, point at it, change it through the same actions with
the same outcomes, and follow guides that wait on what really happens. The starter surface is a
small board of notes; it is there to be replaced.

## Start

```sh
go mod tidy
go run github.com/hollis-labs/substrate/cmd/substrate pins sync --app .
go mod tidy
cd frontend
npm install
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run build
cd ..
go build -o {{ .inputs.repo_name }} ./cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}
./{{ .inputs.repo_name }} identity setup --username owner
./{{ .inputs.repo_name }} serve --managed
```

Commit `go.sum` and `frontend/package-lock.json`. See `docs/identity-bootstrap.md` for scoped
keys and `docs/runbook.md` for installed operation.

## The model

With no model configured the app runs and the agent panel says no model is connected. To
connect one, set the app's block in the operator configuration (the `SUBSTRATE_CONFIG` file):

```yaml
{{ .inputs.repo_name }}:
  agent:
    model: <the model's name or the gateway's alias>
    base_url: <an Anthropic-compatible base URL; requests go to <base_url>/v1/messages>
    key_file: <a file holding the key>
```

The key is read from its file on each request and never reaches the page, a log or the
conversation. Each signed-in person has their own thread; it is kept in `agent.db` in the
data directory, beside the app's database. The agent's routes are under `/api/agent` and need
`{{ .inputs.repo_name }}.read` or `{{ .inputs.repo_name }}.write`, like the rest of the API.

## Your domain

These files are yours. `folio sync` never writes them, whatever has happened to them or to the
preset (its sync policy is `skip`):

- `frontend/src/domain/**`: the surface. `index.ts` exports `SURFACE`, `labels`, `Surface` (the
  view on the left of the workspace) and `context` (what the model sees with each message).
  Replace the notes board with your own thing and keep those exports.
- `cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/prompt.go`: the agent's prompt.
- `README.md`: this file.

These are the preset's, and `folio sync` brings them up to date when the preset changes (if you
edit one, sync reports a conflict instead of overwriting it):

- `cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/agent.go`: mounts the agent host at `/api/agent`.
- `frontend/src/pages/workspace.tsx`: the workspace page (surface, guide bar, agent panel,
  attention layer).
- `frontend/src/ade/**`: the hub, the agent session, guide persistence and the guide events the
  agent is told about.

Everything else comes from the Substrate app layers, with their own sync rules. Run
`folio inspect .` to see how the project stands against the preset and `folio sync . --plan`
to see what a sync would do.
